{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git log --date=short --pretty='%h %ad %s' -- Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md && git log --format= --numstat -- Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md | awk '{a+=\"'$1;d+=$2;n++} END {print \"GDD changed commits/files=\"n,\"added=\"a,\"deleted=\"d}'\"' && git log --format='%h %s' -- Assets/NoSafeCircle | sed -n '1,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"01102b8 2026-08-21 Clarify Frost Field cursor placement\n2b084d1 2026-08-21 Add streaming verification refinement and closure fixes\n01458e7 2026-08-20 Clarify GDD gameplay contracts and prototype ownership\n0808d6a 2026-08-20 Gdd Changes, merged reconcile gdd content into gdd\n938e6de 2026-08-20 Harden verification semantics and coverage\n852d08c 2026-08-20 Close verification ownership and process gaps\nd8a6a89 2026-08-20 Clarify restart, victory, and navigation ownership\nf6fe091 2026-08-19 Clarify build, navigation, feedback, and graph prerequisites\ne1bc32a 2026-08-19 Clarify shared gameplay ownership and reconciliation boundaries\n649a3bc 2026-08-19 Clarify enemy target loss and accessible door targeting\nde86121 2026-08-19 Add requirement representation taxonomy\n85226d4 2026-08-13 Changed GDD to be 2.5 dimension camera and use PixelLab\n2b86e68 2026-08-06 Adding RAG doc\nGDD changed commits/files=13 added=466 deleted=117\n86af98f Harden canonical scene path and asset identity checks\n484e66a Centralize the authoritative DoorPrototype scene\n96dc7be Make camera validation tests non-destructive\n20c5228 Assignment 6 - GER\n0bd74f6 Assignment 5: Add goal-oriented coding agent\n7475170 Assignment 3 - BUILD AN AGENT CREW\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,360p' Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md && sed -n '1,300p' Assignment6GER/RUNTIME_FEEDBACK_HISTORY.md && jq '.' Assignment6GER/outputs/final_result.json Assignment6GER/outputs/final_result_before_runtime_feedback.json 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,360p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,360p' Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md && sed -n '1,300p' Assignment6GER/RUNTIME_FEEDBACK_HISTORY.md && jq '.' Assignment6GER/outputs/final_result.json Assignment6GER/outputs/final_result_before_runtime_feedback.json 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,360p'\"","aggregated_output":"# Assignment 6 — Build a GER Pipeline for Your Capstone\r\n\r\n**Student:** Vincent Liguori  \r\n**Game:** No Safe Circle  \r\n**Assignment:** Assignment 6 — Build a GER Pipeline for Your Capstone\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nFor Assignment 6, I built a GER pipeline that generates, evaluates, refines, and, if necessary, escalates Unity implementation work for **No Safe Circle**.\r\n\r\nRather than creating new agents from scratch, I reused systems from earlier assignments:\r\n\r\n- **Assignment 5** selects what feature should be built next.\r\n- The **Assignment 5 implementation agent** acts as both the **Generator** and the **Refiner**.\r\n- The **Assignment 3 validation infrastructure** acts as the **Evaluator**.\r\n- Assignment 6 adds the **GER orchestration**, a game-specific evaluator contract, runtime-feedback handling, and a **Circuit Breaker**.\r\n\r\nThis made Assignment 6 a continuation of the earlier agent work instead of a separate demo.\r\n\r\n## What Content Does the Pipeline Generate?\r\n\r\nThe pipeline generates **Unity implementation code for missing No Safe Circle features**.\r\n\r\nAssignment 5 had already analyzed the current game against the GDD and produced a list of candidate goals. Instead of regenerating that expensive analysis, I added a lightweight reselection step that reused the saved Assignment 5 artifact and excluded the already-completed Mana goal.\r\n\r\nThe next selected goal was:\r\n\r\n> **Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup**\r\n\r\nThe goal was to replace the disposable perspective test camera with the fixed orthographic isometric presentation required by the GDD.\r\n\r\n## GDD Rule Enforced by the Evaluator\r\n\r\nThe Assignment 6 Evaluator enforces a specific No Safe Circle GDD rule rather than performing only generic code validation.\r\n\r\nFor this run, the camera implementation had to satisfy these requirements:\r\n\r\n1. The gameplay Main Camera uses **orthographic projection**.\r\n2. The game maintains a **consistent isometric viewing orientation**.\r\n3. The player cannot freely rotate the world view.\r\n4. The implementation stays inside the selected camera/projection task instead of expanding into unrelated systems such as Tilemaps, spells, enemies, or sprite sorting.\r\n\r\nA script compiling successfully was not enough to pass.\r\n\r\n## GER Architecture\r\n\r\n```text\r\nAssignment 5 Goal Selection\r\n        ↓\r\nnext_goal_selection.json\r\n        ↓\r\nAssignment 5 Implementation Agent\r\n        ↓\r\nGENERATOR\r\n        ↓\r\nAssignment 3 Validation Infrastructure\r\n        ↓\r\nEVALUATOR\r\n      /       \\\r\n   PASS       FAIL\r\n    ↓           ↓\r\nUnity Test   Assignment 5 Implementation Agent\r\n                ↓\r\n             REFINER\r\n                ↓\r\n             EVALUATOR\r\n                ↓\r\n        repeated failures\r\n                ↓\r\n         CIRCUIT BREAKER\r\n                ↓\r\n           Human Review\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe Circuit Breaker allows a maximum of **three refinement attempts**. If the system cannot self-correct within that limit, the task is escalated for human review.\r\n\r\n## What Happened During the Run\r\n\r\n### Implementation Pass 1 — Generator\r\n\r\nThe Assignment 5 implementation agent generated the first camera implementation.\r\n\r\nIt modified:\r\n\r\n- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs`\r\n- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs`\r\n\r\nThe implementation changed the camera to orthographic and added tests.\r\n\r\n### Evaluation Pass 1 — Static Pass\r\n\r\nThe Evaluator found that the implementation satisfied all four static acceptance criteria:\r\n\r\n- orthographic projection,\r\n- fixed isometric presentation,\r\n- no free camera rotation,\r\n- correct scope.\r\n\r\nHowever, the checked-in Unity scene was still stale, so I rebuilt the Door Prototype scene in Unity and tested the result manually.\r\n\r\n### Unity Runtime Test 1 — Failure\r\n\r\nThe camera was orthographic, but the game was not usable:\r\n\r\n- the camera faced the wrong direction;\r\n- the camera did not follow the player;\r\n- the static evaluator had interpreted “fixed camera” too narrowly.\r\n\r\nI recorded this as:\r\n\r\n`Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback000.json`\r\n\r\nThe pipeline was updated so human Unity runtime failures could re-enter the GER loop as evaluation feedback.\r\n\r\n### Implementation Pass 2 — Refiner\r\n\r\nThe Assignment 5 implementation agent was reused as the Refiner.\r\n\r\nIt created:\r\n\r\n- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/IsometricCameraFollow.cs`\r\n\r\nand modified the scene builder and camera tests.\r\n\r\nThe camera could now translate with the player while preserving a fixed isometric orientation.\r\n\r\n### Evaluation Pass 2 — Static Pass\r\n\r\nThe Evaluator again passed the implementation statically.\r\n\r\nI rebuilt and tested the scene in Unity again.\r\n\r\n### Unity Runtime Test 2 — Failure\r\n\r\nThe camera still did not frame the game correctly. The player-follow behavior existed, but the viewing side and framing were wrong and the starting door was no longer properly visible.\r\n\r\nI recorded this separately as:\r\n\r\n`Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback001.json`\r\n\r\nRuntime feedback files are preserved as an append-only history:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nruntime_feedback000.json\r\nruntime_feedback001.json\r\nruntime_feedback002.json\r\n...\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Implementation Pass 3 — Refiner Made No Progress\r\n\r\nThe Refiner reported `implemented`, but it made **no observed changes under `Assets/`**.\r\n\r\nThis exposed a weakness in the original Assignment 5 implementation contract: Assignment 5 expected an `implemented` result to always include modified files and would crash otherwise.\r\n\r\nFor Assignment 6, I changed that behavior. A no-op refinement is now treated as a **failed repair attempt**, not a pipeline error.\r\n\r\nThe GER progress guard detected the no-op and forced the loop to continue instead of accepting a false success.\r\n\r\n### Implementation Pass 4 — Final Refinement\r\n\r\nThe final allowed refinement modified the scene builder and its tests again. The Evaluator verified the current camera implementation and the additional regression safeguards.\r\n\r\nThe implementation now used:\r\n\r\n- orthographic projection,\r\n- a consistent isometric orientation,\r\n- camera translation/follow without free rotation,\r\n- stable camera-to-player offset behavior,\r\n- tests for camera framing and fixed rotation,\r\n- a regression check for invalid/null follow targets.\r\n\r\nThe Evaluator returned PASS.\r\n\r\nAt this point, all **three allowed refinements** had been used. If the feature had failed again, the Circuit Breaker would have escalated the task to human review.\r\n\r\n## Final Unity Validation\r\n\r\nAfter the final GER pass, I rebuilt the Door Prototype scene in Unity and tested the result manually.\r\n\r\nThe camera now behaves as intended: it uses a **Diablo / Ultima Online-style orthographic isometric presentation**, follows the player appropriately, and does not allow free camera rotation.\r\n\r\nI then ran the relevant Unity automated tests:\r\n\r\n- the full `DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests` EditMode suite;\r\n- the existing `DoorInteractionPlayModeTests` PlayMode suite.\r\n\r\n**All tests passed.**\r\n\r\n## Did the Pipeline Catch Something I Would Have Missed?\r\n\r\nYes.\r\n\r\nThe most useful result of this assignment was discovering that a static evaluator can prove that code satisfies a written requirement while the actual game can still be broken.\r\n\r\nThe first camera implementation passed static evaluation because it was orthographic and used a fixed isometric rotation. In Unity, however, it faced the wrong direction and did not follow the player.\r\n\r\nThe second implementation also passed static evaluation but still framed gameplay incorrectly.\r\n\r\nHuman Play Mode testing exposed those failures. The failures were converted into structured runtime feedback and fed back into GER so the Refiner could continue working on the same selected goal.\r\n\r\nThe pipeline also caught a different failure during Pass 3: the Refiner made no code changes even though unresolved runtime feedback existed. A GER progress guard rejected that no-op repair and counted it toward the Circuit Breaker instead of allowing the pipeline to fail silently.\r\n\r\n## Important Output Artifacts\r\n\r\nThe Assignment 6 run preserves the complete history of the experiment under:\r\n\r\n`Assignment6GER/outputs/`\r\n\r\nImportant artifacts include:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nger_contract.json\r\n\r\nimplementation_pass_1.json\r\nimplementation_pass_2.json\r\nimplementation_pass_3.json\r\nimplementation_pass_4.json\r\n\r\nevaluation_pass_1.json\r\nevaluation_pass_2.json\r\nevaluation_pass_3.json\r\nevaluation_pass_4.json\r\n\r\nruntime_feedback000.json\r\nruntime_feedback001.json\r\n\r\nfinal_result.json\r\nfinal_result_pass_*.json\r\n\r\nevaluator_agent_log_pass_*.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis history makes it possible to reconstruct what each agent did, what failed, what feedback was provided, and how the implementation changed.\r\n\r\n## Final Result\r\n\r\nThe GER pipeline successfully demonstrated all four required behaviors:\r\n\r\n- **Generator:** produced Unity implementation code for the selected No Safe Circle feature.\r\n- **Evaluator:** checked the implementation against a specific rule from the No Safe Circle GDD.\r\n- **Refiner:** repeatedly used evaluator and Unity runtime feedback to repair the implementation.\r\n- **Circuit Breaker:** bounded the loop to three refinement attempts and would have escalated to human review if the final attempt failed.\r\n\r\nThe selected camera feature ultimately passed both the GER Evaluator and real Unity validation.\r\n# Runtime Feedback History Patch\r\n\r\nRuntime feedback is now append-only.\r\n\r\nFiles are preserved as:\r\n\r\n- `runtime_feedback000.json`\r\n- `runtime_feedback001.json`\r\n- `runtime_feedback002.json`\r\n- ...\r\n\r\nA numbered runtime feedback file is never overwritten by `ger_pipeline.py`.\r\n\r\nFor the current second Unity failure, run:\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\ndocker compose run --rm claude python3 Assignment6GER/ger_pipeline.py --runtime-feedback Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback001.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nFuture Unity failures should be recorded as the next sequential file and passed\r\nexplicitly with `--runtime-feedback`.\r\n\r\nIf an unnumbered feedback file is ever supplied, the pipeline automatically\r\ncopies it into the next available numbered history file before refinement.\r\n{\n  \"game\": \"No Safe Circle\",\n  \"selected_goal\": {\n    \"name\": \"Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup\",\n    \"description\": \"Replace the disposable perspective test camera with a fixed orthographic isometric camera configuration matching the GDD's Diablo-1/Ultima-Online-inspired fixed 2.5D isometric presentation.\"\n  },\n  \"gdd_rule_id\": \"gdd-fixed-orthographic-isometric-camera\",\n  \"status\": \"accepted_static\",\n  \"reason\": \"The implementation passed the Assignment 6 static GDD-specific Evaluator. If this run followed human runtime feedback, the developer must now test the refined result again in Unity.\",\n  \"implementation_passes\": 4,\n  \"refinements_used\": 3,\n  \"circuit_breaker\": {\n    \"max_refinements\": 3,\n    \"refinements_used\": 3,\n    \"tripped\": true\n  },\n  \"latest_implementation\": {\n    \"status\": \"implemented\",\n    \"selected_goal_name\": \"Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup\",\n    \"selected_goal_description\": \"Replace the disposable perspective test camera with a fixed orthographic isometric camera configuration matching the GDD's Diablo-1/Ultima-Online-inspired fixed 2.5D isometric presentation.\",\n    \"implementation_summary\": \"Inspected the working tree and confirmed the camera implementation from the prior refinement pass (orthographic projection, fixed 30/-45/0 rotation, constant world-space follow offset via IsometricCameraFollow, viewport-framing tests) is present and already satisfies all four evaluator acceptance criteria. Since the pipeline's guardrail specifically failed pass 3 for making no observed Assets/ changes, this pass made a concrete, in-scope repair addressing the evaluator's own compile_risks note about the fragile BuildPlayer-before-BuildCamera ordering dependency: (1) added an explanatory comment at the Build() call site documenting why that order matters, (2) changed BuildCamera to emit a Debug.LogWarning if ever invoked with a null follow target instead of silently placing the camera at the world origin (which would silently violate the 'consistent isometric presentation' criterion if the ordering were ever broken by a future edit), and (3) added a new EditMode regression test that invokes BuildCamera directly with a null target and asserts the warning fires via LogAssert.Expect, locking this defensive behavior in. No camera projection, rotation, offset math, or scope was changed - the fix hardens the existing correct implementation against future regressions rather than altering its already-passing behavior.\",\n    \"files_created\": [],\n    \"files_modified\": [\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n    ],\n    \"tests_added\": [\n      \"BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing — invokes the private BuildCamera(Transform) method via reflection with a null target and asserts (via LogAssert.Expect) that a warning is logged, and that a valid orthographic Main Camera is still created.\"\n    ],\n    \"validations\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Manual re-read of edited files\",\n        \"status\": \"passed\",\n        \"details\": \"Re-read DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs and DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs in full after edits; confirmed the new comment, null-guard warning, using UnityEngine.TestTools import, and new test are syntactically consistent with the existing code style and asmdef references (NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor.asmdef already references UnityEngine.TestRunner, which provides UnityEngine.TestTools.LogAssert).\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"git diff review vs HEAD\",\n        \"status\": \"passed\",\n        \"details\": \"git diff confirms the working tree's DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs differs substantially from the committed HEAD version (which still has the old perspective camera at (0,8,-8) rotated (45,0,0) with no follow behavior), and my new edits are layered on top of that already-corrected in-scope isometric camera code.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Unity compile / EditMode Test Runner\",\n        \"status\": \"not_available\",\n        \"details\": \"No Unity executable is available in this container; could not run the Editor or Test Runner.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"unity_run_status\": \"not_available\",\n    \"manual_unity_validation\": [\n      \"Open the project in Unity 6000.1.8f1.\",\n      \"Run menu 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' to regenerate the still-stale checked-in DoorPrototype.unity scene from the current builder script.\",\n      \"Open Window > General > Test Runner, switch to EditMode, and run all tests in NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor — confirm all DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests pass, including the new BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing test.\",\n      \"Enter Play Mode and visually confirm the Main Camera is a fixed orthographic isometric view that translates with the player but never rotates, with the player and starting door both comfortably framed at scene start.\"\n    ],\n    \"requirements_satisfied\": [\n      \"Camera remains orthographic with a fixed isometric rotation (30, -45, 0) that is never modified after scene build, matching the GDD's Diablo 1 / Ultima Online-style fixed 2.5D presentation.\",\n      \"Camera position is driven by IsometricCameraFollow using a plain constant world-space offset captured once, decoupled from rotation, so no free camera rotation is possible.\",\n      \"Addressed the evaluator's compile_risks note about the fragile BuildPlayer-before-BuildCamera build ordering by documenting it and making the failure mode observable (a warning) instead of a silent mis-framing bug.\",\n      \"Added a genuine, concrete, in-scope test/code change this pass (satisfying the Assignment 6 refinement-progress guardrail that failed on the prior no-op pass), without altering or re-broadening the already-passing camera behavior.\"\n    ],\n    \"remaining_work\": [\n      \"A human must regenerate the checked-in DoorPrototype.unity scene via the 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' menu command in a real Unity Editor, since hand-editing scene YAML is disallowed and this static pass cannot run Unity.\",\n      \"A human must run the EditMode Test Runner (and ideally Play Mode) in real Unity to confirm the new BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing test and all existing camera tests actually pass, since no Unity executable was available in this environment to verify compilation or test execution.\"\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"This was a REFINE pass per the selected-goal contract's assignment6_refinement_instruction. The prior pass (pass 3) had already produced correct camera code that passed all four evaluator acceptance criteria, but the pipeline's own guardrail failed that pass specifically because it made no observed changes under Assets/. Rather than re-deriving the already-correct camera math or expanding scope, this pass made a small, targeted, camera-scoped hardening change directly responsive to the evaluator's own compile_risks commentary, so the guardrail's 'concrete progress' requirement is met with real, defensible, in-scope work rather than a cosmetic re-save.\",\n    \"assignment6_ger_role\": \"refiner\",\n    \"assignment6_pass_number\": 4,\n    \"observed_assets_delta\": {\n      \"created\": [],\n      \"modified\": [\n        \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n        \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n      ],\n      \"deleted\": []\n    },\n    \"assignment6_refinement_noop\": false\n  },\n  \"latest_evaluation\": {\n    \"status\": \"pass\",\n    \"summary\": \"Pass-4 refinement of the Fixed Isometric Camera goal is verified against the current code. The camera-position/rotation math that resolves the human runtime_feedback (stable world-space offset (10,10,-10) decoupled from rotation, fixed (30,-45,0) orientation, viewport-framing test replacing the flawed forward-points-at-player test) was already independently re-verified by the prior evaluation pass and remains byte-for-byte unchanged in this pass. This pass's own concrete delta — a build-order comment, a null-follow-target Debug.LogWarning fallback in BuildCamera, and a new regression test (BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing) — is present in the actual files, matches implementation_result.json's claims exactly, and is camera-scoped only. All four acceptance criteria pass with concrete evidence, no free-rotation code exists anywhere in Assets/, no scope expansion into Tilemap/sprite-sorting/spells/enemies is present, and the GDD's 'fixed isometric, no free player rotation' rule (No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md:221) is preserved while the camera-follow translation stays within the allowed camera slice per the contract's own scope note.\",\n    \"criteria_results\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"orthographic_projection\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.BuildCamera() sets camera.orthographic = true and camera.orthographicSize = IsometricOrthographicSize (8f) at Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:136-137. IsometricCameraFollow.cs (the only other script that touches the camera GameObject) only ever writes transform.position in LateUpdate (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:25-30) and never touches the Camera component's orthographic flag.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"consistent_isometric_presentation\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"cameraObject.transform.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(IsometricCameraEulerAngles) with IsometricCameraEulerAngles = (30,-45,0) is set once in BuildCamera() (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:22,139) and never modified afterward; IsometricCameraFollow.LateUpdate only writes position (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:25-30). Position is targetPosition + a plain constant IsometricCameraOffset (10,10,-10) (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:29,149) captured once by IsometricCameraFollow.Initialize and reapplied every frame (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:19-23,29), so position is decoupled from rotation rather than derived from camera.forward, which was the specific human runtime_feedback defect. This offset/rotation combination was independently hand-verified against the player (0,1,-4) and door (0,0,0) positions in the prior evaluation pass, landing both inside the required 0.1-0.9 viewport bounds with positive depth, and is exercised at runtime by the still-present Build_MainCamera_FramesPlayerAndStartingDoorInView test (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:132-156). Neither the offset, rotation constants, nor this test were touched in this pass.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"no_free_camera_rotation\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Grepped every script under Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts for Camera/Rotate/mouseX/mouseY/Input.GetAxis references; only IsometricCameraFollow.cs matches, and it exclusively writes transform.position in LateUpdate (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:25-30), never rotation. Build_MainCamera_TranslatesWithPlayerButRotationStaysFixed (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:174-197) asserts rotation is byte-for-byte unchanged after the player moves and LateUpdate runs. No input-driven or orbit-style rotation code exists anywhere in the project.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"selected_goal_scope\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"implementation_result.json's files_modified for this pass are limited to DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs and DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs; direct inspection confirms the only substantive change is a build-order comment (lines 66-69), a null-target Debug.LogWarning fallback inside BuildCamera (lines 141-146), and one new test (BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing, tests file lines 199-222). No Tilemap authoring, sprite-sorting, spell, or enemy code appears anywhere in the diffed files. The camera-follow translation behavior (IsometricCameraFollow) predates this pass and is explicitly permitted camera scope per ger_contract.json's own verification note.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"blocking_issues\": [],\n    \"compile_risks\": [\n      \"None newly introduced this pass. The new test's LogAssert.Expect call relies on UnityEngine.TestTools, which the test asmdef already references via UnityEngine.TestRunner (NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor.asmdef); the file's `using UnityEngine.TestTools;` import (line 7) is present and consistent. IsometricCameraFollow (unqualified reference at DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:151) resolves via C#'s enclosing-namespace lookup from NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Editor up to NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype, the same pattern already used for PlayerMovement/PlayerHealth/etc. in this file, so no new using-directive risk exists.\",\n      \"Unverifiable without a real Unity Editor: actual compilation and EditMode Test Runner execution were not run in this environment (correctly disclosed as unity_run_status = not_available).\"\n    ],\n    \"non_blocking_notes\": [\n      \"The checked-in DoorPrototype.unity scene is stale relative to the current builder script per the project's no-hand-edited-scene-YAML rule; implementation_result.json correctly discloses this as remaining_work requiring a human to run 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' and the EditMode/Play Mode Test Runner in real Unity.\",\n      \"This pass's claim that the pre-existing pass-3 camera math was already correct is consistent with the independent viewport-math verification recorded in evaluation_pass_3.json, so relying on that prior verification here (rather than re-deriving it) is reasonable and not an unsupported claim.\",\n      \"No claim of Unity compilation, Play Mode, or Test Runner execution is made anywhere in implementation_result.json; all such items are honestly marked not_available/remaining_work, consistent with the GER instructions.\"\n    ],\n    \"files_reviewed\": [\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/ger_contract.json\",\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/implementation_result.json\",\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/evaluation_pass_3.json\",\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/implementation_pass_3.json\",\n      \"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/IsometricCameraFollow.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor.asmdef\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.asmdef\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"completed_at_utc\": \"2026-08-19T01:49:04.296412+00:00\",\n  \"runtime_feedback_used\": {\n    \"status\": \"needs_changes\",\n    \"source\": \"human_unity_runtime_validation\",\n    \"summary\": \"The second camera implementation still fails in Unity. The camera follows the player, but its viewing side/framing is wrong and the starting door is no longer properly visible.\",\n    \"developer_interpretation\": \"The camera should remain a separate Main Camera with a target reference to the player. It should follow the player by maintaining a stable world-space isometric offset rather than continually deriving its position so that camera.forward points directly at the player. The fixed offset and viewing orientation must frame the player and the gameplay space ahead, including the starting door.\",\n    \"blocking_issues\": [\n      {\n        \"issue\": \"The camera is positioned on the wrong side of the player and no longer frames the starting door correctly.\",\n        \"required_fix\": \"Choose the correct stable isometric world-space offset/orientation so that the player and the starting door/gameplay space are visible from the intended side.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"issue\": \"The follow implementation derives camera position from camera rotation so that camera.forward points directly at the player. This satisfies the static direction test but produces incorrect gameplay framing.\",\n        \"required_fix\": \"Use a stable world-space follow offset from the player. Translate that offset with the player while keeping orthographic projection and isometric rotation unchanged.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"issue\": \"The evaluator test that verifies camera.forward points at the player is insufficient to establish correct gameplay framing.\",\n        \"required_fix\": \"Replace or supplement that test with checks for a stable player-to-camera offset and fixed rotation. Runtime framing of the player and door must still be confirmed in Unity.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"runtime_feedback_history\": [\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback000.json\",\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback001.json\"\n  ],\n  \"final_result_history\": [\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/final_result_pass_002.json\"\n  ],\n  \"evaluator_log_history\": [\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/evaluator_agent_log_pass_3.json\",\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/evaluator_agent_log_pass_4.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"game\": \"No Safe Circle\",\n  \"selected_goal\": {\n    \"name\": \"Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup\",\n    \"description\": \"Replace the disposable perspective test camera with a fixed orthographic isometric camera configuration matching the GDD's Diablo-1/Ultima-Online-inspired fixed 2.5D isometric presentation.\"\n  },\n  \"gdd_rule_id\": \"gdd-fixed-orthographic-isometric-camera\",\n  \"status\": \"accepted_static\",\n  \"reason\": \"The implementation passed the Assignment 6 static GDD-specific Evaluator. Unity runtime validation is still a human follow-up.\",\n  \"implementation_passes\": 1,\n  \"refinements_used\": 0,\n  \"circuit_breaker\": {\n    \"max_refinements\": 3,\n    \"refinements_used\": 0,\n    \"tripped\": false\n  },\n  \"latest_implementation\": {\n    \"status\": \"implemented\",\n    \"selected_goal_name\": \"Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup\",\n    \"selected_goal_description\": \"Replace the disposable perspective test camera with a fixed orthographic isometric camera configuration matching the GDD's Diablo-1/Ultima-Online-inspired fixed 2.5D isometric presentation.\",\n    \"implementation_summary\": \"Modified DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.BuildCamera() (the sole method responsible for the Main Camera in the door prototype scene) to replace the perspective test camera with a fixed orthographic isometric camera. The camera now sets `Camera.orthographic = true` with an `orthographicSize` of 8, and uses a fixed transform (position (10,10,-10), rotation Euler(30,45,0)) — the classic 30/45 dimetric isometric angle consistent with the GDD's Diablo 1 / Ultima Online-inspired presentation and with Unity's conventional \\\"Isometric Z as Y\\\" tilemap authoring angle referenced in the GDD's Runtime Implementation section. No rotation-input or camera-follow component was added, so the camera transform stays hard-fixed by the scene builder and cannot rotate freely — matching the candidate's \\\"fixed\\\" requirement. No Tilemap authoring or sprite-sorting work was touched, per the candidate's explicit scope exclusion. The disposable primitive Floor/Walls/Door/Player test room was left untouched as the visual verification target, also per scope.\",\n    \"files_created\": [],\n    \"files_modified\": [\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n    ],\n    \"tests_added\": [\n      \"Build_MainCamera_IsFixedOrthographicIsometric — asserts camera.orthographic is true, orthographicSize > 0, camera rotation matches the fixed 30/45/0 isometric angle (not the old perspective angle), and no Rotate/Orbit-named component is attached to the camera hierarchy.\",\n      \"Build_RunTwice_MainCameraStaysSingleAndFixed — asserts re-running the scene builder does not duplicate the Main Camera and it remains orthographic.\"\n    ],\n    \"validations\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Manual code review of full diff\",\n        \"status\": \"passed\",\n        \"details\": \"Reviewed git diff (with -w to filter pre-existing CRLF/whitespace noise across the whole file) and confirmed the only functional change is BuildCamera() switching to orthographic + fixed isometric rotation/position, plus two new constants and two new tests. No other methods or files touched.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"git diff --check (whitespace)\",\n        \"status\": \"not_available\",\n        \"details\": \"The file already has CRLF line endings tracked in git prior to this change (confirmed by lines far outside my edit, e.g. line 1 'using System.IO;', also flagging as trailing-whitespace), so git diff --check output is dominated by pre-existing formatting, not a regression introduced here. Not a meaningful signal for this change.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Unity Test Runner (Editor tests)\",\n        \"status\": \"not_available\",\n        \"details\": \"No Unity executable is present in this container (searched PATH and filesystem for a Unity binary; none found), so DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests could not actually be executed. Tests were written to compile against the existing project APIs/patterns already used elsewhere in the same test file (e.g. GameObject.Find, SerializedObject) but have not been run.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"unity_run_status\": \"not_available\",\n    \"manual_unity_validation\": [\n      \"Open the project in Unity 6000.1.8f1, run menu 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene'.\",\n      \"Confirm the Main Camera's Inspector shows Projection = Orthographic, Size = 8, and Transform rotation = (30, 45, 0), position = (10, 10, -10).\",\n      \"Confirm the Scene/Game view shows the disposable Floor/Walls/Door/Player test room framed from a fixed isometric-style angle (not a top-down perspective view), and that no drag/orbit interaction rotates the Game view camera at runtime.\",\n      \"Run the Unity Test Runner (Edit Mode) on DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests and confirm all tests pass, including the two new camera tests.\",\n      \"Re-run the scene builder a second time and confirm only one Main Camera exists afterward (no duplicate).\"\n    ],\n    \"requirements_satisfied\": [\n      \"Perspective test camera at (0,8,-8) rotated (45,0,0) replaced with an orthographic camera.\",\n      \"Camera uses a fixed isometric angle (30/45 dimetric) and fixed position, matching the GDD's Diablo 1 / Ultima Online-inspired fixed 2.5D isometric presentation.\",\n      \"Camera transform is hard-coded by the scene builder with no rotation-input/orbit component, so it cannot rotate freely.\",\n      \"Change is scoped to camera projection/transform only — no Tilemap authoring or sprite-sorting configuration was added.\",\n      \"Existing disposable primitive Floor/Walls test room left in place as the visual verification target, unchanged.\"\n    ],\n    \"remaining_work\": [\n      \"Human/Unity execution: open the project in the Unity Editor, run the scene builder, and visually confirm the isometric framing against the existing test room (cannot be done in this container without a Unity executable).\",\n      \"Human/Unity execution: run the Edit Mode Test Runner to confirm the two new camera tests and existing tests pass.\"\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"The whole DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs file appears heavily modified in a plain `git diff` only because it is tracked with CRLF line endings that read as full-file trailing-whitespace/line changes to git's default diff; `git diff -w` isolates the real change to the intended ~18-line camera edit plus the doc comment/constants. This CRLF condition predates this task and was left untouched. Orthographic size (8) and camera offset distance (10,10,-10) were chosen to keep the existing disposable Floor (20x20 units)/Walls/Door/Player test room framed in view for visual verification; these are reasonable defaults for a fixed isometric camera and are not part of any GDD-specified numeric requirement, so a human may want to tune them once real isometric Tilemap art exists in a later task.\",\n    \"assignment6_ger_role\": \"generator\",\n    \"assignment6_pass_number\": 1,\n    \"observed_assets_delta\": {\n      \"created\": [],\n      \"modified\": [\n        \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n        \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n      ],\n      \"deleted\": []\n    }\n  },\n  \"latest_evaluation\": {\n    \"status\": \"pass\",\n    \"summary\": \"The Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup goal is correctly implemented in DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.BuildCamera(): the camera is switched to orthographic projection with a fixed 30/45/0 dimetric rotation and fixed position, no rotation-input or orbit component is introduced anywhere in the codebase, and the diff is scoped strictly to the camera plus its new test coverage — no Tilemap, sprite-sorting, spell, or enemy work was absorbed. All four contract criteria pass with concrete code evidence.\",\n    \"criteria_results\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"orthographic_projection\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:117 sets `camera.orthographic = true;` and line 118 sets `camera.orthographicSize = IsometricOrthographicSize;` (8f, defined line 25) inside BuildCamera(), replacing the previous perspective camera entirely — no perspective-only fields (fieldOfView) are set.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"fixed_isometric_presentation\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:23-24 defines `IsometricCameraEulerAngles = (30,45,0)` (classic dimetric isometric angle) and `IsometricCameraOffset = (10,10,-10)`; BuildCamera() (lines 110-122) applies these as a hard-coded fixed transform (`cameraObject.transform.position = IsometricCameraOffset; cameraObject.transform.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(IsometricCameraEulerAngles);`), replacing the prior perspective test angle noted in the contract (0,8,-8)/(45,0,0). This is a static, code-authored fixed isometric framing, not a runtime-computed or player-adjustable one.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"no_free_camera_rotation\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"BuildCamera() only assigns a Camera and AudioListener component to the camera GameObject (lines 112-115) and sets a fixed transform once at scene-build time; no orbit/rotation/look controller is attached. A project-wide grep for `Camera|orthographic` across all .cs files under Assets/ returns matches only in DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs and its test file — no separate camera-control or input-rotation script exists. PlayerMovement.cs (Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerMovement.cs) only reads WASD keys to move the CharacterController via `controller.Move(...)`; it never touches Camera or Transform.rotation of the camera. The new test `Build_MainCamera_IsFixedOrthographicIsometric` (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:95-116) also asserts no attached component has 'Rotate' or 'Orbit' in its type name.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"selected_goal_scope\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"implementation_result.json's files_modified lists exactly DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs and DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs. Reading the full scene builder file confirms BuildCamera() is the only method changed for this goal; BuildFloor()/BuildWalls()/BuildDoor()/BuildPlayer()/BuildUI() (primitive test-room and UI) are unchanged and still use disposable primitives — no Tilemap, sprite-sorting, spell, or enemy code was added, matching implementation_scope's 'Single behavior: correct fixed isometric camera setup only.'\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"blocking_issues\": [],\n    \"compile_risks\": [\n      \"None found: BuildCamera() uses only standard UnityEngine.Camera/Transform/Quaternion APIs already imported at the top of the file, and the new test methods use only APIs (SerializedObject, GetComponentsInParent<Behaviour>, Quaternion.Angle) consistent with existing usage elsewhere in the same test file.\"\n    ],\n    \"non_blocking_notes\": [\n      \"The checked-in Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity still serializes the old perspective camera (`orthographic: 0`, `field of view: 60`, rotation ~45° tilt) because the scene is