{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find Pipeline -type f | rg -v 'ArchitectureReview/outputs|Reconciliation/outputs|__pycache__' | xargs rg -n \\\"GitHub|worktree|lease|claim|heartbeat|Draft PR|merge queue|gh |Issue|idempot|reconcile\\\" | sed -n '1,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md:5:`AgentInvocationRequest` describes one generic bounded invocation: run identity, role, prompt, repository context, semantic capabilities, write policy, output shape, capability-class selection, budgets, and provider configuration. It has no No Safe Circle task identity and no dependency on `Tasks/*.yaml`. `AgentResult` describes only an invocation outcome and provider/agent claims. Task identity belongs to `Pipeline/TaskExecution`; delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, integration, repository changes, command execution, and test success remain decisions for higher deterministic repository, test, and evidence systems.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md:13:`ProviderOutputInvalid` represents provider output from which an adapter could not produce a structured-output candidate. `AgentRunner` normalizes it to `schema_error`. This is distinct from a successfully parsed candidate that the runner later rejects through central schema validation, although both outcomes normalize to `schema_error`. `ProviderRequestRejected` represents a provider that cannot safely honor a selected request policy and normalizes to `invalid_request` after provider/model selection. Exact provider raw output is retained in `provider.log` when it is valid. Neither exception establishes deterministic correctness, delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, approval, integration, or test-success authority.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md:21:Claude receives the exact concrete configured model with no alias or fallback, native `--max-turns` equal to the request's required positive `turn_limit`, and the independent external hard `timeout_seconds` enforced by the shared subprocess transport. The prompt travels through stdin, while the compact output schema, exact `--tools` value, and explicit `Bash`, `Edit`, `Write`, `NotebookEdit`, `WebSearch`, and `WebFetch` denial travel as direct argv elements with `shell=False`; no `--allowedTools` argument is emitted. The shared standard-library transport captures stdout and stderr concurrently through `communicate`, creates a new process group/session, terminates the group on timeout with bounded cleanup, and preserves available partial output. Deterministic adapter and AgentRunner integration tests inject a fake process runner and never launch Claude. The opt-in `tests/claude_repository_read_search_live_smoke.py` requires `NSC_RUN_CLAUDE_REPOSITORY_SMOKE=1`; normal deterministic runs skip live Claude access.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md:31:Every failed `AgentResult` has a non-whitespace, non-authoritative `failure_message` and must keep `structured_output` null so rejected output cannot appear accepted; successful results leave the diagnostic null or empty. This diagnostic preserves configuration, provider-exception, schema-validation, and rejected-metadata details. It never establishes delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, test success, or approval. Provider invocation failures and structured-output validation are normalized separately: unexpected ordinary provider exceptions are `internal_error`, while invalid structured JSON or schema mismatch is `schema_error`. Provider responses are field-snapshotted exactly once after their exact-type check. Structured output is immediately detached and frozen, and that same snapshot is both schema-validated and retained. Valid usage and execution/change/test claims survive a post-invocation `schema_error`, while rejected structured output remains null. Invalid raw logs are replaced by an empty log and a safe diagnostic; malformed exception text cannot block artifact publication. Process-control exceptions are not swallowed.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:218:            response.claimed_changed_paths,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:220:            response.claims_execution_occurred,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:221:            response.claimed_test_commands,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:232:                raise ContractValidationError(\"claimed_changed_paths must be an array\")\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:234:                raise ContractValidationError(\"claimed_test_commands must be an array\")\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:259:                    metadata_result.claimed_changed_paths, duration,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:261:                    metadata_result.claims_execution_occurred,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:262:                    metadata_result.claimed_test_commands,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:271:                frozen_output, metadata_result.claimed_changed_paths,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:273:                metadata_result.claims_execution_occurred,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py:274:                metadata_result.claimed_test_commands,\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:365:    claimed_changed_paths: tuple[str, ...]\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:369:    claims_execution_occurred: bool\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:370:    claimed_test_commands: tuple[str, ...]\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:440:            \"claimed_changed_paths\",\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:441:            _path_tuple(self.claimed_changed_paths, field=\"claimed_changed_paths\"),\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:455:        if not isinstance(self.claims_execution_occurred, bool):\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:456:            raise ContractValidationError(\"claims_execution_occurred must be boolean\")\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:459:            \"claimed_test_commands\",\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contract